NEARS-1397 finding (LOW, non-blocking, breaks_ac=false)
Where: UserApp/lib/features/auth/widgets/sign_in/manual_login_widget.dart
       EmailOrPhoneLoginField.build -> inputFormatters: isPhone ? [FilteringTextInputFormatter.allow([0-9])] : null
       manual_login_widget onChanged reverse branch: (text.contains('@') || text.contains(notNumberRegExp)) && isNumberLogin

Live observation (emulator-5558):
 phone mode, field = "1501234567", keyboard up
 -> typed 'a'  : field stayed "1501234567" (filtered)
 -> typed '@'  : field stayed "1501234567" (filtered), still +971 phone mode
 -> cleared to empty : flipped back to EMAIL mode (picker +971 gone, "Email/Phone" placeholder), keyboard stayed up
 -> email mode typed "a@b" : landed unfiltered (email mode, no formatter)

Impact: the onChanged reverse-toggle branches (contains('@') / contains(non-digit)) are unreachable while in phone
mode because the digit-only inputFormatter strips those chars before onChanged sees them. Reverse email<-phone works
ONLY by clearing the field. Divergence from legacy CustomTextField combined field (fixed emailAddress keyboard, no
digit filter) where typing '@' flipped back. Does NOT block login (user clears to switch) and does NOT affect the
TB1/AC3 keystroke/keyboard/focus retention, which is fully fixed. Suggest: either drop the now-dead onChanged reverse
branches, or defer the digit-only filter until phone mode is confirmed, if mid-field reverse is desired.
